 "poem": "The Spirit, who kept not them alive,\nWas weeping on the dead and dying,\nAnd hid His face from all unseen.\nTo him was drawn the holiest seen,\nFor that His spirit came again,\nFor He had trod our buried.\nBut the Lord, the manhood divine,\nWhom they worshiped for their sacrifice,\nNot now is He the demon.\nHushed were the murmurs of everyone,\nNo more he held a mystery high\nWho walked among men quietly.",
